  "en": {
   "title": "US Northeast freezing level: 0 °C from 1,936 ft to 6,037 ft, snow line up to 4,921 ft (10 November)",
   "description": "The 0 °C level in the US Northeast, next days: 1,936 ft (590 m) to 6,037 ft (1,840 m). Warmest hours: snow line about 984 ft (300 m) lower, up to …",
   "lede": "The 0 °C level in the US Northeast, next days: 1,936 ft (590 m) to 6,037 ft (1,840 m). Warmest hours: snow line about 984 ft (300 m) lower, up to 4,921 ft (1,500 m) at Stratton on Tuesday 10 November. The model is right more often than a hunch, and less often than we would like.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "The 0 °C level, daily",
     "p": [
      "The 0 °C level at the resorts below, from the coldest to the warmest hour of each day: Tuesday 10 November: from 2,756 ft (840 m) to 5,971 ft (1,820 m). Wednesday 11 November: from 2,461 ft (750 m) to 4,003 ft (1,220 m). Thursday 12 November: from 1,936 ft (590 m) to 6,037 ft (1,840 m)."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Snow line by resort",
     "p": [
      "Whiteface Mountain (base 1,220 ft (372 m), top 4,373 ft (1,333 m)): snow line about 4,265 ft (1,300 m) on 10 November, mid-mountain. Snow above, rain or wet snow below.",
      "Stratton (base 1,991 ft (607 m), top 3,881 ft (1,183 m)): snow line about 4,921 ft (1,500 m) on 10 November, above the top. The whole mountain is in the rain-or-wet-snow zone if precipitation falls.",
      "Okemo Mountain, base 1,158 ft (353 m), top 3,320 ft (1,012 m): snow line near 4,593 ft (1,400 m) on 10 November, over the top of the lifts; rain or wet snow everywhere if anything falls.",
      "Magic Mountain (base 1,378 ft (420 m), top 2,851 ft (869 m)): snow line about 4,921 ft (1,500 m) on 10 November, above the top. The whole mountain is in the rain-or-wet-snow zone if precipitation falls."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Rain-on-snow risk",
     "p": [
      "Rain-on-snow risk in the next days: none that we can see. The snow line stays low enough on the wet days.",
      "Tug Hill (1,706 ft (520 m)): 15 mm forecast, snow line near 1,378 ft (420 m) while it falls.",
      "The forecast gives Stowe (4,393 ft (1,339 m)) 16 mm of precipitation, with the snow line near 2,100 ft (640 m) during the wet hours."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "The 0 °C level and the snow line, briefly",
     "p": [
      "The short version: colder up high, melting starts at the 0 °C level, rain only some 984 ft (300 m) lower, because melting takes time. That gap is the snow line. In dry air, evaporation adds extra cooling and the line can drop further."
     ]
    }
